 17592186409702 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409708 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409703 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409708 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409705 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409708 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409706 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409708 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409708 1077 "selection" 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409708 1078 #edb/ref 17592186409702 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409708 1079 #uuid "0677d12a-c058-55e0-b0e6-dbd13fd6e32a" 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409709 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409698 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409709 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409699 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409709 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409701 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409709 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409704 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409709 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409707 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409709 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409709 1077 "selection" 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409709 1078 #edb/ref 17592186409698 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409709 1079 #uuid "6c28df82-226c-551a-9267-de3801bebac5" 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409710 1068 #edb/ref 17592186409708 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409710 1069 "q-105422" 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409710 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409710 1071 "Which of the following sets are neither open nor closed?\n\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,2\\le x\\le 4,\\,0<{y}^{2}\\le 5}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<7}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,1\\le x<4,\\,{y}^{2}<9}$" 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409710 1072 #uuid "4c5afa8a-a09e-5d94-9d6f-17bde8db6cd3" 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409710 1074 "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(2,\\sqrt{5}).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(3,0).$\n\n- The second set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (the corresponding inequality is strict).\n\n- The third set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(1,0).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(4,0).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409711 1068 #edb/ref 17592186409709 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409711 1069 "q-161644" 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409711 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409711 1071 "Which of the following sets are open?\n\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }-2\\le x\\le 0,\\,1\\le y\\le 2-x}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }-1<x<1,\\,0<y<1+x}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }4\\le {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 9}$" 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409711 1072 #uuid "b04f2bd5-de84-5515-a0a5-3d6c81e3d583" 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409711 1074 "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\n- The second set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The third set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409712 1062 #uuid "32d95962-0b06-593e-ac0e-b990be203765" 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409712 1063 #edb/ref 17592186278582 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409713 1058 #edb/ref 17592186409712 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409713 1062 #uuid "74b478c0-0d6d-5f2e-ad2f-087dc00a6757" 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409713 1063 #edb/ref 17592186409711 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409714 1058 #edb/ref 17592186409713 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409714 1062 #uuid "7cb34581-54b6-5401-9371-c9018f69c37a" 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409714 1063 #edb/ref 17592186241054 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409715 1058 #edb/ref 17592186409714 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409715 1062 #uuid "86912f04-287b-5201-a438-59ef54ae3dde" 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409715 1063 #edb/ref 17592186409710 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409716 1058 #edb/ref 17592186409715 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409716 1062 #uuid "cbd6fa81-f968-55ac-9411-91ed05e75b0f" 13194139533580 17592186045417 true] [17592186409716 1063 #edb/ref 17592186338994 13194139533580 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-dc8bf892-7626-53fb-8653-56fbe0502566" 17592186409697 "answer-0dbcbe48-2124-5037-bac0-c99498ef9fe0" 17592186409698 "answer-3a63ced9-ca36-5f7e-b7b0-e658c1fa60dd" 17592186409699 "answer-3fc08d88-96fa-5f9d-8557-7fd8fe262961" 175